@juanwilliams3423 Beat me to it. And we haven't even seen the full effect of his destruction. He continues to arrest our cheap labor workforce. He continues to alienate our trade partners. And he continues to gut the agencies and regulations that protect our fragile economy. The effects of those horrific policies take a while to kick in, but they are coming.

And STILL the Republicans in Congress sit on their hands. Even if all those policies were reversed tomorrow, their effect would still negatively impact our economy for quite some time. And the repair period would take much longer. My guess is the economy will still be bottoming out come midterms.

It remains to be seen if the Republicans are going to be able to cheat enough to counteract that. Their problem now is that, historically, they have been cheating and gerrymandering so much, for decades, there's not a whole lot of room left to cheat much more.

